Boxer for AROS @VERSION@ (@ABI_NAME@, x86_64)
=============================================

This is a TEST BUILD of the AROS port of Boxer, the DOS game emulator
front end by Alun Bestor, with Boxer's DOSBox 0.74 core. It is not a
release. Expect missing features and bugs.

This build only runs on @ABI_NAME@. Binaries for ABIv11 (AROS One) and for
mainline AROS (ABI v1) are different files and do not run on each other.

Installing
----------
1. Unpack the archive where you want Boxer to live, for example SYS:
   or Work:. From a Shell:
     UnZip <archive>.zip -d SYS:      (or: LhA x <archive>.lha SYS:)
   This makes the drawer "Boxer". You can rename or move it later, but
   then run Install-Assign again (step 3).
   Keep these next to BoxerUI: Fonts/, conf/ and dosbox.msg.

2. Open the Boxer drawer in Wanderer.

3. Double-click "Install-Assign". A window shows what it does and stays
   open until you close it. It:
     - assigns Boxer: to this drawer for the running system;
     - writes S:Boxer-Assign, one Assign line pointing at this drawer;
     - adds a block of five lines, from ";BEGIN Boxer" to ";END Boxer",
       to S:User-Startup, so Boxer: is set again after every reboot.
       S:User-Startup is created if your system has none; lines already
       in it are kept. Running Install-Assign again adds nothing twice.
   Game icons need Boxer:, because their default tool is Boxer:BoxerUI.
   If Boxer: already points to another drawer, a requester asks whether
   to replace it; nothing is changed without your answer.
   From a Shell instead:
     CD SYS:Boxer
     Execute Install-Assign
   (add KEEP or REPLACE to answer the question in advance).

4. Double-click BoxerUI. On the first start Boxer proposes a folder for
   your DOS games and one for their saved games; confirm or choose your
   own. Then import a game. Each imported game gets an icon in the games
   folder; double-click it to play.

From a Shell BoxerUI needs a larger stack:
  Stack 65536
  BoxerUI

Uninstalling
------------
1. In a Shell: CD to the Boxer drawer, then
     Execute Install-Assign REMOVE
   This deletes S:Boxer-Assign and removes the Boxer: assign. The block
   in S:User-Startup then does nothing; to remove it too, open
   S:User-Startup in an editor and delete the lines from ";BEGIN Boxer"
   to ";END Boxer".
2. Delete the Boxer drawer. Your games folder and its "Boxer Data"
   (saved games) are separate; delete them only if you no longer want
   them. Boxer's settings are in ENVARC:Boxer.

Before you start
----------------
This is an EXPERIMENTAL PREVIEW. Use a separate test installation of AROS,
or a copy of your system, not the one you depend on: a hung game session
can take the whole AROS system down when it is closed (see Known issues).

Known issues
------------
Tested on ABIv11 (AROS One) only, under QEMU. Mainline AROS (ABI v1) has
not been tested with this package.

Not tested in this package's acceptance runs: paths that contain spaces,
importing from LhA archives, and keeping icons that a game folder already
has. They may work; nobody has checked them for this build.

- Loading a Tyrian save from the game's title screen froze the game with
  noise on the screen, twice, on ABIv11. Loading the same save through the
  in-game Options menu worked. That is the path that was checked, not a
  workaround known to avoid every freeze. The same game copy and save
  loaded fine in a Mac build of Boxer on DOSBox Staging; that is a
  comparison, not a confirmed cause.
- After such a freeze, quitting the session caused a DOSBox assertion
  (CPU_IRET, cpu.cpp:901) and, separately, a crash in the SDL audio
  thread. These are two separate events and neither is explained yet.
  Closing a hung session can crash the whole AROS system.
- The session froze twice at the end of a game installer (when the
  installer exited) on a machine with live audio output. Eight later
  attempts did not freeze. How often it happens is not known.
- Tyrian's first title menu may ignore keys and clicks until its demo has
  run once (observed; cause not known).

When something goes wrong
-------------------------
BoxerUI writes a log, by default to RAM:boxerui.log. Each start of BoxerUI
(also "Launch game" and every game icon) starts the log again, and
everything in RAM: is lost when AROS restarts or crashes. If Boxer hangs
or takes the system down, the RAM: log is usually gone by the time you
look for it.

To keep the log on disk from the start, choose a drawer you can write to.
The Boxer drawer itself may be read-only, or on a read-only installation,
so do not rely on it; Work: is a common choice. Then either:
  - select the BoxerUI icon, choose Information from the Icon menu and
    add the ToolType
      LOG=Work:boxerui.log
    (game icons use it too), or
  - from a Shell:
      Stack 65536
      BoxerUI LOG Work:boxerui.log
The log on disk is also restarted by each start of BoxerUI, so copy it
away before you try again.

If Boxer is still on screen but seems hung:
1. Open a second Shell (Wanderer menu, or Right-Amiga+W).
2. Copy the log somewhere that survives a restart, for example:
     Copy RAM:boxerui.log Work:boxerui-1.log
3. Type Status to list running programs; note whether BoxerUI is there.

Please send: the log file, what you did just before (which screen, which
button or key), the AROS version and distribution (Kickstart/Workbench
version from the Wanderer "About" window), the ABI (ABIv11 or mainline),
the amount of RAM, whether it runs on real hardware (which) or in an
emulator (which, with its settings), and the BoxerUI sha256 from
SHA256SUMS in this drawer.

What the system must have
-------------------------
See REQUIREMENTS.txt. No game data and no DOS games are included.

